    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d11-a6">

                <pb facs="0208" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv08/pg198"/>

                <head>Annex D to HD–52</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation<anchor n="11" xml:id="d11-f1"
                    />]</seg></opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">delegation of
                            the<lb/>kingdom of the serbs, croats<lb/>and slovenes</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-09-10">September 10, 1919</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. President</hi>: Referring to my letter of this
                    morning, I have the honor to inform Your Excellency that the Royal Government
                    has just resigned, and that this delegation feels itself obliged, therefore, to
                    await from the new Government the authorization to sign the treaty of peace with
                    the Austrian Republic.</p>
                <p>Please accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. Pachitch</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Georges
                            Clemenceau</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">President of the Peace
                            Conference,<lb/>Quai d’Orsay.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
